{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-nucleon-borromean-topology","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:nucleon-borromean-topology","kind":"lemma","title":"Nucleon Borromean topology and Hopf-link binding","proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-nucleon-borromean-topology"],"tags":["nucleon","borromean","hopf-link","color-exchange"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.HadronicMass.nucleon_borromean_topology","text":"nucleon-borromean-topology.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/nucleon-borromean-topology.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:nucleon-borromean-topology\"></a><p><em>The proton and neutron are Borromean configurations (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6_2^3</code>) of three quark vortices. They are internally bound by Hopf links <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{Hopf}}</code>. Since <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Vol}(\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{Hopf}}) = 0</code>, the mass contribution arises entirely from the Skein functional.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/nucleon-borromean-topology.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Lemma","number":"16.7.1"}
